# Toolchain & Project Structure

## Language

**C11** (`-std=c11`). **No C++.**

## Compiler flags (from `Makefile`)

```
-std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror
-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L
-Iinclude
-O2          # release (CFLAGS)
```

When the `_O_BINARY` probe succeeds, the Makefile also adds:

```
-DHEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO   # _setmode() + _O_BINARY on stdin/stdout/opened FILEs
```

No extra libraries are linked on any platform (`LDFLAGS` stays empty).

Debug target uses `CFLAGS_DEBUG`: `-g -O1 -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer`.
When `HEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO` is set, `-fsanitize=…` is dropped (UCRT64 gcc ships no
AddressSanitizer runtime), leaving `-g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer`.

## Artefact layout

All build outputs live under **`build/`**; never write binaries at the repo root
or into `tests/`.

| Artefact | Path |
|----------|------|
| Release binary | `build/head-toto` (`.exe` on Windows) |
| Debug binary | `build/head-toto-debug` |
| Main objects | `build/*.o` (from `src/*.c`) |
| Test binary | `build/tests/test_core` |
| Test objects | `build/tests/*.o` (from `tests/*.c`) |
| Test fixtures | `build/tests/fixture_*.tmp` (created and removed by tests) |

`build/.gitkeep` and `build/tests/.gitkeep` keep the directories in git when empty.
`make clean` removes objects, binaries, and fixtures but leaves the `.gitkeep` files.

## Compiler selection

`Makefile` picks **gcc** if available, else **clang**:

```makefile
CC := $(shell command -v gcc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo gcc || echo clang)
```

On **`OS=Windows_NT`**, if `C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/gcc` exists, it becomes `CC`
(so Git Bash does not use a minimal or unrelated MinGW toolchain).

## Platform probe (`_O_BINARY`)

Before compiling, the Makefile preprocesses:

```c
#include <io.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
#ifndef _O_BINARY
#error no _O_BINARY
#endif
```

- **Probe fails** → plain POSIX I/O in `head_toto_io.c` / `head_toto_run.c`.
- **Probe succeeds** → `-DHEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO`; stdin/stdout switched to binary
  mode and FILEs opened with `_O_BINARY`, so byte counts and CRLF are preserved.

Typical outcomes:

| Environment | Probe | I/O mode |
|-------------|-------|----------|
| Linux / WSL | fail (no `<io.h>`) | POSIX `open`/`read`/`write` |
| MSYS2 UCRT64 gcc | success | POSIX calls + binary mode |
| Git Bash + UCRT64 gcc | success | POSIX calls + binary mode |
| Cygwin / MSYS runtime gcc | fail* | POSIX `open`/`read`/`write` |

\*The Cygwin/MSYS runtimes are already binary by default; the plain POSIX path is correct there.

## Build system

**GNU Make** at repo root. Object files are compiled into `build/` and
`build/tests/`, then linked.

| Target | Output |
|--------|--------|
| `make` / `all` | `build/head-toto` |
| `make debug` | `build/head-toto-debug` |
| `make test` | builds + runs `build/tests/test_core` |
| `make clean` | removes objects/binaries/fixtures under `build/` (keeps `.gitkeep`) |
| `make install` | `install -m 755 build/head-toto /usr/local/bin` (Linux/macOS) |

**Main sources:** `src/main.c`, `src/head_toto_emit.c`, `src/head_toto_cli.c`,
`src/head_toto_count.c`, `src/head_toto_io.c`, `src/head_toto_run.c`

**Test sources:** `tests/test_runner.c`, `tests/test_count_parse.c`,
`tests/test_copy_lines.c`, `tests/test_copy_bytes.c`,
`tests/test_elide_lines.c`, `tests/test_elide_bytes.c`

## Dependencies

- **All builds:** libc only (`unistd.h`, `fcntl.h`, `sys/stat.h`, `string.h`,
  `stdint.h`, `stdlib.h`, `errno.h`, etc.).
- **Windows binary-mode builds:** libc + `<io.h>` (`_setmode`) — still no extra link libraries.

